            <ArticleTitle>Acetylcholine-induced coronary microvascular vasospasm in a patient with angina pectoris and normal coronary angiogram--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>995-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We demonstrated a continuous intracoronary infusion of acetylcholine-induced marked decrease of coronary blood flow estimated by intracoronary Doppler flow wire without significant epicardial coronary narrowing. This case can be called a patient with microvascular vasospastic angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
